        "id": 1003571
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-10-14T20:23:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Are these flags used somewhere? I would expect them to be processed by OPEN?",
      "revId": "8ebf2606db64b33be13eafe3bbfd0640992c7ac5",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a835e0c3_5694479c",
        "filename": "src/include/nfsv41.h",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 1560,
      "author": {
        "id": 1038782
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-10-15T13:35:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, currently, the enum values are defined but not yet processed. \n\nAccording to RFC 9754, when a client requests delegation timestamps via the\nOPEN4_SHARE_ACCESS_WANT_DELEG_TIMESTAMPS flag, the server MUST set the\nappropriate delegation type in the response:\n- OPEN_DELEGATE_WRITE_ATTRS_DELEG (5) for write delegations\n- OPEN_DELEGATE_READ_ATTRS_DELEG (4) for read delegations\n\nI need to implement below pieces of code:\n1. Checking for OPEN4_SHARE_ACCESS_WANT_DELEG_TIMESTAMPS in get_delegation().\n2. Upgrading the delegation type when the flag is set and client is NFSv4.2.\n3. Updating all delegation code paths to handle the new types (state_deleg.c,\n   nfs4_state.c, commonlib.c).",
      "parentUuid": "7f68430a_9f984346",
      "revId": "8ebf2606db64b33be13eafe3bbfd0640992c7ac5",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
